      "content": "It's possible that root vegetables might be affected if the damage is underground. However, if you're solely dealing with leaf damage, chemicals like thrips or spider mites aren't always easy to eradicate. There are some harder-to-see pest killers like cherry or red pepper sprays, or you could use a natural solution like horticultural oil. For tomato plants, you can try classified fumigants like Thimet or Thinsulate which can help to control pests that hide. In severe cases, professional help might be needed to assess and remedy the issue. Make sure to keep washing hands regularly and don’t eat the plants until you're sure they're safe—you wouldn’t want to consume any pesticides inadvertently!",
